{
  "title": "OpenHealth \u2014 healthcare (3,896\u2605)",
  "content": "Project: OpenHealth\nDomain: healthcare | Scale: medium | Stars: 3,896\nProblem: OpenHealth helps users take charge of their health data by consolidating personal health information and leveraging AI to provide personalized health insights and management assistance. It enables private, locally-runnable health management with data privacy as a core principle.\nTarget users: Individual health-conscious users, Patients managing chronic conditions, Users seeking personalized health insights, Privacy-focused health data managers\nCore features: Centralized Health Data Input; Smart Data Parsing & Standardization; Contextual AI Conversations; Multi-LLM Support (GPT, Claude, Gemini, LLaMA, DeepSeek, Ollama); Multi-language Support; Health Data Visualization\nIntegrations: OpenAI GPT, Anthropic Claude, Google Gemini, Meta LLaMA, DeepSeek-V3, Ollama (local LLM), Apple Health, Google Fit, Oura Ring, Whoop, Garmin, Vercel Blob Storage, Trigger.dev, Amplitude Analytics\nTech stack: Next.js 15, React 19, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS, Shadcn UI, Framer Motion + Next.js API routes, Node.js, TypeScript + Prisma ORM + Docker/Podman, Vercel deployment, Trigger.dev for job execution\nKey libraries: LangChain (multi-LLM framework), LangSmith (LLM debugging), Next-Auth 5 (authentication), Next-intl (internationalization), React-PDF & pdf2pic (document processing), Zod (schema validation), SWR (data fetching)\nArchitecture: monolith\nDesign lessons:\n- Privacy-first design: Application supports fully local execution with Ollama and local parsing via Docling, minimizing cloud dependencies\n- Multi-modal LLM integration: Abstraction layer via LangChain enables flexible switching between commercial and open-source models without vendor lock-in\n- Polyglot processing: Python-based data parsing (planned TypeScript migration) decoupled from Next.js frontend, showing phased modernization strategy\n- User-centric internationalization: Early i18n support across 9+ languages indicates global health market ambitions from MVP stage",
